@*
    A question that has to be answered before anything else happens.

    Two things in the app are worth stopping someone for: deleting an empire, and leaving one with
    changes that have not been saved. Both are cheap to ask about and expensive to get wrong, and
    neither has an undo behind it.

    The buttons are the caller's, because the answers are not always yes and no — leaving with
    unsaved work has three sensible ones, and calling any of them "Cancel" would be a poor
    description of what it does.
*@

@*
    Stopped at the backdrop as well, because there may be a dialog under this one: the lite editor
    is itself a dialog on the list, and a press that carried on up dismissed the question and closed
    the empire behind it from the one click.
*@
<div class="sem-modal" @onclick="Dismiss" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
    @*
        Clicks inside the sheet are stopped from reaching the backdrop, which would otherwise read
        every press of a button as a press on the backdrop as well and close the dialog underneath
        whatever was clicked.
    *@
    <div class="sheet" role="alertdialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="@_titleId"
         tabindex="-1" @ref="_sheet" @onkeydown="OnKey" @onkeydown:stopPropagation="true"
         @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
        <h2 id="@_titleId">@Title</h2>

        @if (Message is { Length: > 0 })
        {
            <p>@Message</p>
        }

        <div class="choices">
            @ChildContent
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private ElementReference _sheet;

    /// <summary>Ties the sheet to its heading for a screen reader, uniquely on a page.</summary>
    private readonly string _titleId = $"confirm-{Guid.NewGuid():N}";

    /// <summary>The question, as a heading.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public required string Title { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What the answer will mean, where that is not obvious from the question.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Message { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The answers, which the caller supplies as buttons.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public required RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Called when the dialog is dismissed rather than answered.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnDismiss { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Takes the keyboard when the dialog appears, so that Escape reaches it and Tab stays among
    /// the answers rather than wandering the page behind.
    /// </summary>
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender)
        {
            await _sheet.FocusAsync();
        }
    }

    private Task OnKey(KeyboardEventArgs e) =>
        e.Key == "Escape" ? Dismiss() : Task.CompletedTask;

    private Task Dismiss() => OnDismiss.InvokeAsync();
}
